er_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"The neighbourhood_evolution analysis (step_01) shows a sharp, full change (peak_change = 1.0) at time 77986 with disjoint contact lists before and after, indicating an abrupt turnover. I controlled for alternative explanations: total activity drops after the change (step_02), and the popular nodes lists before/after (steps 03 and 04) show different activity patterns that could partially explain partner shifts; additionally, static neighbour lists over the combined half-windows (step_05) show many connections when time is ignored, so static connectivity alone cannot explain the timed abrupt switch. Taken together the temporal evidence supports a regime switch in the group's contacts around 77986 rather than slow background turnover.\"\n}", "total_input_tokens": 64705, "total_output_tokens": 4489, "total_tokens": 69194, "total_latency_ms": 53613, "llm_calls": 17, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}